# class Above { constructor() { takesUnfinishedHeir(this) } get x() { } get y() { } }; class Heir extends Above { x = 1 }; takesHeir(new Heir): until the field is defined a read of x finds the getter above.
# Each is handed to a helper of its own, and the question is asked of the type that flow proves for the helper's parameter.
# Where a read can run nothing but getters that a class defines for good, the getters stand in place of the answer.
# At the call the operand's own type has none of what flow proves of an array, a Map, a Set or an instance of one class of several. The entry parameter of the callee has.
